issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nAs of the 1.4.0 release, calling ``Session.identity_key()`` is throwing an AttributeError that looks like typo in the code.\r\nThis relatively minor, and I've updated my application to just use ``sqlalchemy.orm.util.identity_key()`` directly.  But thought was worth filing anyways.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n```py\r\n>>> from sqlalchemy.orm import Session\r\n>>> Session.identity_key(instance=123)\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n  File \"$PYENV/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/orm/session.py\", line 84, in identity_key\r\n    return util.perload.orm_util.identity_key(*args, **kwargs)\r\nAttributeError: module 'sqlalchemy.util' has no attribute 'perload'\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nExpected error to be same as calling calling sqlalchemy.orm.util.identity_key():\r\n\r\n```py\r\n>>> from sqlalchemy.orm.util import identity_key\r\n>>> identity_key(instance=123)\r\n...\r\nsqlalchemy.orm.exc.UnmappedInstanceError: Class 'builtins.int' is not mapped\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Thanks!**","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https:/